// Hard canon: no error-hiding (engineering/dont-hide-errors-with-fallbacks.md).
// A promise `.catch(() => <default>)` swallows the rejection and substitutes a fake value,
// exactly like a fallback default — the failure vanishes and a wrong result ships quietly.
// Let it reject to the route/job error-boundary, or handle the specific error explicitly.
//
// Empty `catch {}` is already banned by Biome's built-in noEmptyBlockStatements (biome.json).
// The semantic `catch { return null/[]/0 }` / `catch { console.error(); continue }` shapes are
// not statically detectable and are caught by the /noslop gate instead.
language js

`$p.catch(() => $body)` where {
  $body <: or {
    JsNullLiteralExpression(),
    JsArrayExpression(),
    JsObjectExpression(),
    JsNumberLiteralExpression(),
    JsStringLiteralExpression(),
    JsParenthesizedExpression(),
    `undefined`
  },
  register_diagnostic(span=$body, message="`.catch(() => <дефолт>)` глушит ошибку — дай промису реджектнуться к error-boundary или обработай конкретную ошибку явно (dont-hide-errors-with-fallbacks).")
}
